-- title:
--   Existence of a function with m ≥ 2g+1 distinct simple poles
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $F$ be a field equipped with a $K$-algebra structure, assumed to be a one-variable function field over $K$ in the sense that some element of $F$ is transcendental over $K$ and makes $F$ finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K$ adjoins that element. Let $m$ be a natural number with $2g + 1 \le m$, where $g =$ `genusFF K F` is the $K$-dimension of $H^1$ of the zero divisor. The assertion is that there exist an element $x \in F$ and an injective family $P : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `Place K F` of places of $F/K$ — each place being a valuation subring of $F$ that is not all of $F$, contains the image of $K$, and is a principal ideal ring — such that: $x$ is transcendental over $K$; $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field generated by $x$ over $K$, of degree exactly $m$; at each of the $m$ places $P_j$ one has $\mathrm{ord}_{P_j}(x) = -1$, where $\mathrm{ord}$ is minus the logarithm of the associated $\mathbb{Z}^{m0}$-valued adic valuation; and $\mathrm{ord}_v(x) \ge 0$ at every place $v$ outside the range of $P$.
--
--   This is the standard construction, via Riemann–Roch in the non-special range, of a function whose pole divisor is reduced (multiplicity one at each of $m \ge 2g+1$ distinct places) and of degree $m$, so that $[F : K(x)] = m$. It supplies the divisor along which the Riemann–Roch normal form of a function field is built, and is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_riemannRochSpace_nsmul_poleDivisor_normalForm`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_riemannRochSpace_nsmul_poleDivisor_normalForm).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_exists_transcendental_reduced_poleDivisor.lean

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_DivisorClassGroup
import Definitions.Def_AlgebraicCurve_Repartitions

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open AlgebraicCurve

universe u v

theorem AlgebraicCurve.exists_transcendental_reduced_poleDivisor
    (K : Type u) (F : Type v) [Field K] [IsAlgClosed K] [Field F] [Algebra K F]
    (hF : ∃ x : F, Transcendental K x ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F)
    (m : ℕ) (hm : 2 * genusFF K F + 1 ≤ m) :
    ∃ (x : F) (P : Fin m → Place K F),
      Function.Injective P ∧ Transcendental K x ∧
      FiniteDimensional (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F ∧
      Module.finrank (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F = m ∧
      (∀ j, (P j).ord x = -1) ∧
      (∀ v : Place K F, v ∉ Set.range P → 0 ≤ v.ord x) := by sorry
